 "method": "Own derivation from linearised Einstein eqs (static s-wave perturbation of the uniform string, gauge c=e=0: sphere radius and g_zz unperturbed). Gauge-invariant first-order 3x3 system for (A,B,P) plus one algebraic constraint; singular points only X=r^n=0,1,inf at every order (no apparent singularity, unlike scalar master eqs). 1/n expansion in horizon variable y=1-r^-n: leading operator triangular, so each order = three 1D integrations; solutions are rational(y) x HPLs with letters {0,1} (own exact HPL algebra). Per order: constraint C_m==0, no ln y at horizon (regularity), no x^p (p<=0) terms at X->inf (decay; far zone contributes beyond all orders) fix c_P, c_S and Lambda_{m-1}. Constants H(w;1) reduced to an MZV basis by own regularised double-shuffle linear algebra (weights<=11). Recursion run to order 11 -> k0..k10. k3,k4 re-derived (not input). No PSLQ/fitting for any coefficient.",
